# Publish safety is enforced by sync_public.py's / sync_forge.py's whitelists,
# NOT by this file or by the absence of a remote — this repo DOES have a git
# remote (origin). Do not add council/ or channel files here. They belong in
# this repo and are kept out of the public one by the whitelist, which cannot
# be forgotten.
.venv-train/
smoke_adapter/
smoke_adapter_*/
dpo_adapter_native/
dpo_adapter/
localllm/out_demo/
localllm/corpus.txt
# Downloaded training TEXT and the model folders trained from it. get_corpus.py
# caches ~200 MB here and the corpus is re-derivable from a named source plus a
# size, so the recipe belongs in git and the bytes do not.
localllm/corpora/
localllm/corpus.previous.txt
localllm/out_*/
*.err
*.log
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
_locallm_publish/

# Imported third-party datasets. These live in the HF cache OUTSIDE this repo on
# purpose; these patterns are the backstop in case anything is ever staged here.
# KodCode-V1 is CC BY-NC 4.0 - it may be used locally to screen candidate tasks,
# but its rows must NEVER be committed to or published from this MIT repo.
# AceCode-89K is MIT and may be redistributed with attribution.
data/kodcode*
data/acecode*
data/imported_*
localllm/out_gui/
# Three l's above is a typo that has been there since the entry was
# written, so the real locallm/out_gui/ was never ignored: 73 MB of
# trained weights sat one `git add -A` away from the repo, against this
# file's own rule that checkpoints are reproducible and do not belong here.
locallm/out_gui/

# The sponsor handoff package is his proprietary guidance. It lives here for
# reading and never enters version control or any publish whitelist.
S12-LOCAL-MODEL-HANDOFF-2026-07-28/

# Replication adapters: same convention as dpo_adapter_native/ above -- the
# weights are reproducible from the code + gated corpus and are hundreds of MB.
# The ANALYSIS of them (compare_adapters.py, init_vs_training.py, the finding)
# is committed; the binaries are not.
poscontrol/adapter_replication/
poscontrol/adapter_replication2/
poscontrol/served/*.gguf

# Positive-control adapter binaries (Aug 20): reproducible from seed+corpus, and the
# safetensors exceed GitHub's 100MB limit. sha256 manifest committed instead (WEIGHTS-MANIFEST.md).
dpo_adapter_poscontrol/*.safetensors
dpo_adapter_poscontrol/export/*.gguf
dpo_adapter_poscontrol/export/amplified/*.safetensors
# Agent session tooling, none of it product
.claude/
.codex/
# pytest's cache, created by running the suite. Not a result.
.pytest_cache/

# --- data and build artifacts, not source -------------------------------
# Corpora are downloaded or derived (get_corpus.py, make_corpus.py) and one
# of them is 190MB, past GitHub's limit. Trained checkpoints and generated
# lowerings are reproducible from the code plus the recorded manifests.
locallm/corpora/
locallm/corpus.txt
locallm/corpus.previous.txt
locallm/training_data_dafny/
locallm/out/
locallm/out-dafny-mps/
# ...but not the evidence. A findings document that cites a table the
# repository does not contain is a claim without a file behind it, and
# `git add t/out/score-r8.md` failed silently for three rounds on 2026-09-19
# because this rule matched before anyone noticed.
#
# The fix written then did not work, and was found on 2026-09-20 still not
# working. `t/out/` excludes the DIRECTORY, and git cannot re-include a file
# whose parent directory is excluded, so every `!t/out/...` line below it was
# inert -- the 25 evidence files in the repository are there because someone
# reached for `-f` anyway. `t/.gitignore` held a second copy of the same
# mistake, one line reading `out/`, which is why `git check-ignore` blamed that
# file rather than this one.
#
# So: exclude the CONTENTS, re-include the directories so git still descends
# into them, and only then name the evidence. Verify with
# `git check-ignore -v t/out/score-r9.md` printing nothing at all.
t/out/**
!t/out/**/
!t/out/score-*.md
!t/out/evaluator-state-*.json
!t/out/capacity-*.json
!t/out/CONSTRAINED-*.md
!t/out/KERNEL-DISAGREEMENT-*.md
!t/out/scorecard-*.json
!t/out/recheck.json
!t/out/spec-disagree.json
# the split IS the held-out set: score_heldout.py defaults to it and
# locallm/ACHIEVEMENTS.md cites it, so a clone without it cannot reproduce
# the headline at all.
!t/out/loop/split-*.json
!t/out/loop/eval-ids.txt
!t/out/loop/train-ids.txt
!t/out/loop/apps-upper.txt
!t/out/loop/sft-r*.jsonl
!t/out/loop/pairs-r*.jsonl
!t/out/spec-experiment/**/WHY-NO-TABLE.md
# tup/book/ stays TRACKED: it is generated, but it is the exact bytes that
# executed, which is evidence a receipt can point at.

# --- working record: private, not product ---------------------------------
